      "text": "First, let's analyze the given problem. The logo consists of a square with 4 circles inside it such that each circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles. The square has a side length of 20 inches. Let's denote the side length of the square as \\( s = 20 \\) inches. The circles are arranged in a \\( 2 \\times 2 \\) grid inside the square.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the radius of the circles\nEach circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles. Let the radius of each circle be \\( r \\). The distance from the center of each circle to the side of the square is \\( r \\). The centers of two adjacent circles are \\( 2r \\) apart horizontally and \\( 2r \\) apart vertically from the centers of the circles they touch.\n\nIf we consider the distance from the center of the square to the center of one of the smaller circles along the diagonal of the square, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\\[\n(2r)^2 + (2r)^2 = 20^2\n\\]\n\\[\n4r^2 + 4r^2 = 400\n\\]\n\\[\n8r^2 = 400\n\\]\n\\[\nr^2 = 50\n\\]\n\\[\nr = \\sqrt{50} = 5\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the area of the square\nThe area of the square is given by:\n\\[\ns^2 = 20^2 = 400 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the area of one circle\nThe area of one circle is:\n\\[\n\\pi r^2 = \\pi (5\\sqrt{2})^2 = \\pi \\cdot 50 = 50\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Calculate the total area of the 4 circles\nThe total area of the 4 circles is:\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 50\\pi = 200\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Calculate the shaded area\nThe shaded area is the area of the square minus the area of the 4 circles:\n\\[\n400 - 200\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nThus, the shaded area is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{400 - 200\\pi}\n\\]",
