      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the area of the squares and circles in Wei's company logo and then find the shaded area. Let's go through the problem step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the side length of the square and the circles\nWei's logo is a square with each side measuring 20 inches. Each circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the side length of the circles\nConsider one of the circles in the logo. The circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles. The distance from the center of each circle to the side of the square is half the side length of the square minus the radius of the circle. This distance is \\(10 - r\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius of the circle.\n\nSince the circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles, the diameter of the circle is equal to twice the side length of the square minus the radius of the circle. Therefore, the diameter of the circle is \\(20 - 2r\\).\n\nThe radius \\(r\\) of the circle can be found by noting that the distance from the center of the circle to the side of the square is half the side length of the square minus the radius of the circle. This distance is \\(10 - r\\), so we have:\n\\[2r = 10 - r\\]\n\\[3r = 10\\]\n\\[r = \\frac{10}{3}\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the area of one circle\nThe area of one circle is given by the formula \\(\\pi r^2\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Area of one circle} = \\pi \\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)^2 = \\pi \\left(\\frac{100}{9}\\right) = \\frac{100\\pi}{9} \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Calculate the total area of the circles\nSince there are four circles, the total area of the circles is:\n\\[\n\\text{Total area of the circles} = 4 \\times \\frac{100\\pi}{9} = \\frac{400\\pi}{9} \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Calculate the area of the square\nThe area of the square is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the square} = 20 \\times 20 = 400 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Calculate the shaded area\nThe shaded area is the area of the square minus the total area of the circles:\n\\[\n\\text{Shaded area} = 400 - \\frac{400\\pi}{9} = \\frac{3600}{9} - \\frac{400\\pi}{9} = \\frac{3600 - 400\\pi}{9} \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\nThe shaded area is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3600 - 400\\pi}{9}}\n\\]",
